Welcome to Broadmayne First School
Our School
The principle aim of our school is to provide a happy, caring and stimulating learning environment, which encourages the love of learning and the fullfillment of potential in each child. Positive relationships are at the heart of all we do, and we strive to ensure that each child is treated as an individual, with his or her specific needs met. It is our belief that all children can excel, hence our school motto 'Flying High'.
Equity of opportunity is central to the ethos and core values of our school. To establish and maintain this, the school is fully committed to:
Each child is helped to acquire the following skills, abilities and qualities, which are fundamental to education and personal growth:
Broadmayne First School has an excellent team of experienced and skilled staff who work harmoniously to provide the best quality education for all pupils, with a focus on supporting the development and wellbeing of all, in a warm, safe environment. We believe children learn best when they have positive relationships with the people around them.
We encourage as much outdoor learning as possible, and believe that this directly contributes to the good progress our children make academically. All of our children look after the environment from Reception onwards, linking this with their work in our generous grounds. Ofsted judged us to be a good school in March 2023 and commented on the caring culture of the school.
We know that we cannot be effective in isolation and we actively seek to connect with our parents and carers, families, and the wider community. The ethos of the school is one of openness, recognising the partnership of parents, pupils, staff and govenors.
